      MOTION TO WITHDRAW CONFIDENTIAL TESTIMONY AND FILE
   AMENDED PUBLIC TESTIMONY OF MICHAEL P. GORMAN ON BEHALF OF
        THE REGENTS OF THE NEW MEXICO STATE UNIVERSITY

       In light of the Stipulation entered by El Paso Electric Company ("EPE") and the Regents

of the New Mexico State University ("NMSU") and filed by EPE on October 28, 2026, NMSU

hereby files this Motion to allow it to withdraw the Confidential Testimony of Michael P. Gorman

and its Confidential Exhibit MPG-21, and to file an amended version of the public Testimony of

Michael P. Gorman that was filed on October 23, 2026 on behalf of NMSU. The Amended

Testimony of Michael P. Gorman would remove the redactions on pages 22, 25, and 27 of Mr.

Gorman's testimony in light of the Stipulation that EPE waives confidentiality of the redacted

material and EPE will not challenge its admission into the evidentiary record in this case. In light

of the Stipulation, NMSU's withdrawal of Mr. Gorman's confidential testimony and filing an

amended, non-redacted version of Mr. Gorman's public testimony would simplify and clarify the

record, and would avoid procedural and evidentiary complexities during the hearing in this matter.

       NMSU contacted other parties in this case for their positions on this Motion, and reports

as follows: EPE and Coalition for Clean Affordable Energy support the Motion; Walmart, the City

of Las Cruces, and Dona Ana County do not oppose the Motion; and no other party responded by

the time of filing this Motion.

       WHEREFORE, for the above reasons, NMSU requests the Hearing Examiners issue an

order allowing NMSU to withdraw the Confidential Testimony of Michael P. Gorman and its
 Confidential Exhibit MPG-21, and to file an amended version of Mr. Gorman's public testimony

without redactions.

                                   Respectfully submitted on October 28, 2026,

